the life of an entrepreneur  i got a question from eric who's one of  my readers who wrote in a huge long  email but basically wanted to know  i know you've been in business since you  were young how has it been  so that's a pretty wide-ranging question  uh  i started my business my first real  company when i was 19  and uh before then i had a whole bunch  of  little things on the side selling  baseball cards and a whole bunch of  different ventures  but the real company was when i was 19.  how has it been uh it's amazing  it's fun it's it's tons of highs and  it's also  frightening and scary and and  you doubt yourself constantly and tons  of lows as well you know it's part  the best part of my life in the worst  part of my life all wrapped into one  and i think any entrepreneur will can uh  can feel the same way i think you can uh  i don't know the word is you can you can  associate with it  maybe will help us to tell you the best  part and the worst part  in my business career the worst was when  i thought about quitting  in the early days of my software company  i had  two partners and and we thought things  would be great you know we thought  we had a great product people loved it  and we would  take over the world with our software uh  and it just never picked up like we  thought it would and things were so much  harder than we thought it would be  and and it's frustrating because you're  losing money you know i'm making 300  bucks a month that wasn't enough to  survive  i was frustrated and angry and and  lost that my confidence and didn't know  where to go with it and and thought  about  giving up on a daily basis um  the worst moment for me in all of that  mess  was i don't remember the day but i was  over at my parents house for a family  function  and i got a call from my business  partner and i took it upstairs  and we just we had struggled so much in  getting to this point and trying to  figure out how we would grow we both had  the same vision what we wanted to do but  but different plans and how  to get there and it got to the point  where i thought you know what this is  this is not working you know i i'm so  frustrated  i don't want to be there i don't want to  be in this business anymore i quit  you know you could buy my shares  whatever it is we'll figure it out but  i'm done i'm done with this company  i need to do something else where more  where my  talents and skills are being used  properly i want to have an impact  i'm done and i hung up the phone and i  cried for 15 minutes  just uncontrollably you know tears  running down my face  down my nose you know it's like i was a  i was a wreck  just a total wreck because i built i  spent so much time building this thing  you know i put so much of myself into it  barely sleeping to launch this company  and  we saw barely any progress it was so  disheartening and my mom came up and she  put her hand on my shoulder and  asked me what was wrong and i couldn't  even say anything you know i was just so  overwhelmed  i don't know if i responded at all  and i went to bed that night you know  cried myself to sleep  and the next day i got up and went back  to work  that's what you do that's what you do as  an entrepreneur  but that was that was the worst single  worst day in my life as an entrepreneur  the best day was when i sold my company  and that wasn't that far from when i  almost gave up you know it was only  two years in between that terrible day  where i almost quit to being acquired  and all the  crazy stuff that happened in between  and what kept me going was was the  passion for the business and feeling  like i was doing something right  and i wasn't doing it just for the money  i was doing it to do it and doing it to  have an impact and doing it to  to be part of something meaningful and  so  as an entrepreneur you have to be you  know willing and ready to ride that  roller coaster you're going to have  great highs when you feel on top of the  world you feel  invincible you feel like yeah this is  working finally you know  this is this is amazing and then  almost as quickly as feeling that  emotion you'll get you'll get hit in the  face with something  and it'll knock you down and you're in  full  crisis mode trying to solve this problem  and and just when you feel like things  couldn't get worse  another punch comes to the stomach and  and you you'll be tested beyond  beyond what you thought was possible  it'll be so bad  and it'll really test your character and  test  to see what you're made of and test how  much  you really love this business or not if  you're doing it for the right reasons or  not  and if you come out on the other side  it's because you're really super  passionate about this company  and not willing to give up so it was a  bit of a broad question so i gave you  kind of a broad answer but that's my  story in a nutshell  if you guys like the video please give  it a thumbs up below i love seeing us  come in and  if you have a specific question for me  or if you want to leave a comment leave  it below  i really love seeing those come in i  really appreciate it when you guys do  that  it really makes me want to keep doing  more of these videos for you  you guys inspire me to keep going so  please leave a comment underneath thank  you so much  and i'll see you soon  you

